    "text": "<p>Consider the following reaction :</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><msubsup><mi>HSO</mi><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo></msubsup><mfenced><mi>aq</mi></mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Electrolysis</mi></mrow><mrow><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Hydrolysis</mi></mrow></mfrac><mn>2</mn><msubsup><mi>HSO</mi><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math></p><p>The dihedral angle in product <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> in its solid phase at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>110</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math> is</p>",
